)`","files":null},{"type":5,"timestamp":1780329367,"nonce":"xHHl5cIkHPj4dgttb/8Bho+T93k=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABEBC1LM8AAAAGGWho-A"},"added":["documentation"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"timestamp":1780329367,"nonce":"vdKdGz1x4uxHE+75avKyaAFEUxE=","metadata":{"github-id":"LE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABEBC1LM8AAAAGGWhpoA"},"added":["deployment"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"timestamp":1780332296,"nonce":"zXYy65Id/v/slNxOcXmjsuR6ULE=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABEdx_ow","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/201#issuecomment-4594630563"},"message":"**Reactive corridor path-adjuster (`rolker/unh_marine_navigation#30` / [PR #51](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_navigation/pull/51)) merged 2026-06-01** (jazzy `5f03356`) — so the \"in flight / not yet landed\" item in the Notes is now landed. Folding its on-water validation in here. The avoider's overlay is always-on; the slow-down is opt-in (off by default).\n\n## Must-verify — survey-line obstacle avoidance (`rolker/unh_marine_navigation#30`)\n\n- [ ] **Reshapes around a real obstacle** — with an obstacle on/near a survey line (present in the local costmap), the boat bends the followed path around it and **re-anchors to the line** afterward, instead of stopping or abandoning the line.\n- [ ] **Clear water = no change** — on lines with no obstacle, the followed path stays identical to the nominal trackline (no spurious wiggle, no extra FollowPath churn).\n- [ ] **Fully blocked = safe degrade** — if the corridor is fully blocked (no feasible detour within `max_deviation`), it passes the nominal path through → reflex Collision-Monitor stop → FollowPath ABORT → recovery → pilot (same as today; it never plans into an obstacle body).\n- [ ] **CAMP overlay renders** — the `survey_obstacle_avoidance` MarkerArray (auto-discovered by CAMP) shows, while deviating: faint nominal line + bright adjusted path + red \"avoiding\" band + an \"AVOIDING\" text flag; it clears when the boat is back on the line. *(This is the concrete overlay behind the \"operator awareness\" item above; needs the bridge from [PR #200](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/200) for OTH.)*\n- [ ] **Obstacle is visible** — enable the `local_costmap/costmap` (OccupancyGrid) grid layer in CAMP so the operator can see the obstacle being avoided alongside the detour.\n- [ ] **Optional slow-down (opt-in)** — `survey_avoidance.avoid_speed` defaults to 0 (off). If set \u003e 0, confirm the boat slows through the detour (the controller derives speed from per-pose timestamps the node writes on the deviating run). Leave off unless wanted.\n\n## Live tuning (do a sim pass first)\n\nEvery tunable is a **live ROS parameter** on the bt_navigator node — adjust without redeploying the BT (rqt_reconfigure groups them under `survey_avoidance`):\n\n```\nros2 param list | grep survey_avoidance\nros2 param set \u003cbt_navigator-node\u003e survey_avoidance.\u003cname\u003e \u003cvalue\u003e\n```\n\nParams: `max_deviation`, `along_track_spacing`, `lateral_resolution`, `line_following_weight`, `obstacle_avoidance_weight`, `smoothness_weight`, `chatter_damping_weight`, `max_lateral_change`, `avoid_speed`. **Key ratio: `line_following_weight` : `obstacle_avoidance_weight`** (hug-the-line vs deviate-around). Defaults (1.0 : 0.02) are unvalidated placeholders.\n\n## ⚠️ Watch out for\n\n1. **Defaults are untuned** — set sane corridor weights in sim against the costmap inflation before trusting them on water; the avoider's behavior is sensitive to the `line_following_weight : obstacle_avoidance_weight` ratio.\n2. **Only ahead-of-boat, in-window** — it reshapes stations ahead of the boat and inside the rolling local-costmap window; obstacles beyond the window aren't acted on until the boat closes in.\n3. **Reflex topics now run full-rate on VPN** (from [PR #200](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/pull/200)) — the collision pointcloud + slowdown/stop polygons lost their 1 Hz VPN throttle (deliberate, to prioritise SA over-the-horizon; the heavy `local_costmap_windowed` kept its 0.5 Hz). **Confirm the camera-segmentation overlays don't visibly suffer** on the OTH/Starlink path now that those run full-rate — if they do, re-throttle the costmap window or a camera stream.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":2,"timestamp":1780334098,"nonce":"uvzN8Q4XmLoiyr7e0MGajywDYy8=","metadata":{"github-id":"RTE_lADOK4fCvM8AAAABEBC1LM8AAAAGGZSH0Q"},"title":"Deployment 2026-06-01: clean survey run — override/resume (#52) + turning limits + cross-track","was":"Deployment 2026-06-01: clean survey run — override/resume (#52) + turning limits + cross-track"}]}